1
00:00:00,667 --> 00:00:01,467
<i> Please give this to Joey.</i>

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:02,867
<i>Are you really sure
about leaving?</i>

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:05,133
<i>I'm needed back home,
unlike here.</i>

4
00:00:05,267 --> 00:00:06,967
<i> Everyone, standby here, okay?</i>

5
00:00:07,100 --> 00:00:09,467
<i>I want you all to welcome
my special guest.</i>

6
00:00:09,600 --> 00:00:10,700
<i> Okay, Madam Delilah.</i>

7
00:00:10,833 --> 00:00:12,400
<i> [SHRIEKS AND GROANS]</i>

8
00:00:12,533 --> 00:00:13,800
<i>- Are you okay?
- No, I'm not!</i>

9
00:00:13,933 --> 00:00:15,600
<i>- Sorry, Miss...
- Zoey.</i>

10
00:00:15,733 --> 00:00:17,067
<i> Francis, owner of this resort.</i>

11
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:18,367
<i> My God, it's fine now.</i>

12
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:19,533
<i> Why do you look so flushed?</i>

13
00:00:19,667 --> 00:00:20,933
<i> You know what? You stay here.</i>

14
00:00:21,067 --> 00:00:22,300
<i>- I'll look for clues.
- You're leaving me here?</i>

15
00:00:22,433 --> 00:00:24,100
<i>- Yes.
- What?</i>

16
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:25,867
<i> Andrew! Andrew, let me in.</i>

17
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,167
<i>I'm really getting annoyed
with you.</i>

18
00:00:27,300 --> 00:00:28,200
<i> Joey, there's a safe here.</i>

19
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:29,433
<i> Try 1-2-3-4.</i>

20
00:00:29,567 --> 00:00:31,100
<i>I already tried that.
Still nothing.</i>

21
00:00:31,233 --> 00:00:34,067
<i>Andrew, come on!
Someone might see us here!</i>

22
00:00:34,233 --> 00:00:35,767
<i> Oh, dear, I knew it.</i>

23
00:00:35,900 --> 00:00:37,633
<i> I forgot something in my safe.</i>

24
00:00:37,767 --> 00:00:38,600
<i> Joey?</i>

25
00:00:38,733 --> 00:00:41,100
<i>Why are you standing
outside my room?</i>

26
00:00:41,233 --> 00:00:43,167
<i>I was looking for my boyfriend.</i>

27
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:46,700
<i>You're so in love
you can't be apart.</i>

28
00:00:46,833 --> 00:00:47,933
<i>Look.
[CLACKS]</i>

29
00:00:48,067 --> 00:00:49,333
<i> Check everywhere!</i>

30
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:51,433
<i>- Well? Did you find anything?
- Ma'am, nothing.</i>

31
00:00:51,567 --> 00:00:53,067
<i> Babe! What are you doing here?</i>

32
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:54,733
<i> That's so sweet.</i>

33
00:00:54,867 --> 00:00:56,133
<i>- Madam Delilah.
- Andrew, Ma'am.</i>

34
00:00:56,267 --> 00:00:58,967
<i>We have to stick
to our characters.</i>

35
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:01,767
<i>Then we have to convince
everyone we really are a couple.</i>

36
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:02,867
<i> I've got an idea.</i>

37
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:04,100
<i> Damn you, Andrew.</i>

38
00:01:04,233 --> 00:01:06,533
<i>This doesn't feel like
pretending anymore.</i>

39
00:01:06,667 --> 00:01:10,900
<i>We've run out of drugs
since Ninong disappeared.</i>

40
00:01:11,067 --> 00:01:14,267
<i>The good news is
we have a new supplier.</i>

41
00:01:15,467 --> 00:01:16,900
<i> [GUN COCKS]</i>

42
00:01:20,600 --> 00:01:22,567
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

43
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:42,900
Babe, are you choosing
between those two?

44
00:01:43,033 --> 00:01:45,767
Yes, I still can't decide.

45
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:47,267
Which one looks better?

46
00:01:48,933 --> 00:01:51,333
Well, I think...

47
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:54,000
Both suit you.

48
00:01:54,133 --> 00:01:58,300
I think you will look beautiful
in both of them.

49
00:01:58,433 --> 00:02:01,500
Well, you're flattering me
again!

50
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:03,233
When have I ever lied to you?

51
00:02:03,367 --> 00:02:05,000
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:02:08,900 --> 00:02:11,000
All right then, Babe.

53
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:12,833
I'll just try on both.

54
00:02:12,967 --> 00:02:14,700
I'll just try
to wear this, so...

55
00:02:14,867 --> 00:02:16,300
- Okay.
- I can't wait.

56
00:02:16,433 --> 00:02:17,867
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

57
00:02:26,867 --> 00:02:29,700
Can we really trust
this contact, Madam Delilah?

58
00:02:31,767 --> 00:02:32,633
Why?

59
00:02:32,767 --> 00:02:35,700
Don't you trust me?
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

60
00:02:35,833 --> 00:02:37,133
Madam...

61
00:02:37,267 --> 00:02:39,067
Of course, it's you
we're talking about.

62
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:39,900
Sure.

63
00:02:40,033 --> 00:02:41,833
You're the boss, Ma'am.

64
00:02:41,967 --> 00:02:43,400
That will never change.

65
00:02:43,533 --> 00:02:44,833
Very good.

66
00:02:44,967 --> 00:02:47,433
When will we meet
this new supplier?

67
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:50,167
Let him meet me first.

68
00:02:50,300 --> 00:02:54,200
I want the boss
to meet the other boss.

69
00:02:55,333 --> 00:02:57,300
[PHONE RINGING]

70
00:02:57,433 --> 00:02:58,633
Oh...

71
00:02:58,767 --> 00:03:00,500
speaking of the devil.

72
00:03:01,800 --> 00:03:03,833
Hello, Friend?

73
00:03:03,967 --> 00:03:06,800
Madam Delilah,
this is just a courtesy call.

74
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:08,600
Why?
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

75
00:03:08,733 --> 00:03:10,400
Are we cancelling?

76
00:03:11,067 --> 00:03:12,167
No, we're pushing through.

77
00:03:12,300 --> 00:03:14,233
I'll be leaving Manila soon.

78
00:03:14,367 --> 00:03:17,933
I thought you backed out.

79
00:03:18,067 --> 00:03:19,733
That would be an insult to you.

80
00:03:19,867 --> 00:03:22,067
<i> I'd never do that to you.</i>

81
00:03:22,233 --> 00:03:25,967
<i>After all, this partnership
is worth the travel.</i>

82
00:03:26,100 --> 00:03:28,600
I'll be there,
and our plan is a go.

83
00:03:28,733 --> 00:03:29,933
Okay.

84
00:03:30,067 --> 00:03:32,367
But, don't worry about anything.

85
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,433
<i> Everything is under control.</i>

86
00:03:34,567 --> 00:03:36,967
There will be no problems here.

87
00:03:37,100 --> 00:03:40,000
Just have a safe trip, okay?

88
00:03:40,133 --> 00:03:41,433
<i> See you.</i>

89
00:03:41,567 --> 00:03:45,567
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

90
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:51,000
Hon, why are you still here?

91
00:03:51,133 --> 00:03:53,300
I thought today was your trip?

92
00:03:53,433 --> 00:03:55,067
I was just waiting for you.

93
00:03:55,233 --> 00:03:57,133
How's mom?

94
00:03:57,267 --> 00:03:59,933
Did you find someone
to watch over her?

95
00:04:00,067 --> 00:04:01,833
Yes, I have.

96
00:04:01,967 --> 00:04:05,167
So, don't worry about us, okay?

97
00:04:05,300 --> 00:04:08,133
Just focus on your meeting.

98
00:04:08,267 --> 00:04:10,333
And thank you for your concern.

99
00:04:10,467 --> 00:04:12,700
- Of course.
- My husband is really so kind.

100
00:04:12,833 --> 00:04:14,167
[CHUCKLES]

101
00:04:15,367 --> 00:04:16,633
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

102
00:04:18,033 --> 00:04:19,433
Delivery!

103
00:04:21,700 --> 00:04:22,600
Here it is, Ma'am.

104
00:04:22,733 --> 00:04:24,233
<i>- Thank you.
- Thank you.</i>

105
00:04:24,367 --> 00:04:25,833
Just count it.

106
00:04:29,100 --> 00:04:30,467
That's my helmet!

107
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:37,567
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

108
00:04:39,333 --> 00:04:42,233
Does this look good on me?

109
00:04:49,333 --> 00:04:51,167
You're ignoring me.

110
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,000
Well, maybe it looks bad.

111
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:56,700
Not really.

112
00:04:57,733 --> 00:05:02,933
And ever since,
everything you wear...

113
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:04,300
looks good on you.

114
00:05:07,267 --> 00:05:10,233
The dress or me?

115
00:05:15,900 --> 00:05:18,467
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

116
00:05:22,667 --> 00:05:25,933
Joey, have you chosen
between the two dresses?

117
00:05:29,533 --> 00:05:31,567
I don't really like them.

118
00:05:31,700 --> 00:05:33,867
Really?

119
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,133
You don't like this?

120
00:05:36,300 --> 00:05:39,233
You're kind of choosy,
aren't you?

121
00:05:39,367 --> 00:05:41,033
Well, there are
plenty of options here...

122
00:05:41,167 --> 00:05:42,667
Like the one I'm wearing.

123
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:44,800
Right, Boss Idol?

124
00:05:44,933 --> 00:05:46,967
- Yes, that looks good.
- See?

125
00:05:47,100 --> 00:05:49,367
Boss Idol likes it.

126
00:05:49,500 --> 00:05:51,233
Really?

127
00:05:51,367 --> 00:05:55,400
Personally,
I don't like it that much.

128
00:05:55,533 --> 00:05:57,900
It looks kind of old-fashioned.

129
00:05:58,033 --> 00:06:01,100
You know? Like it's trying
too hard to stand out

130
00:06:01,233 --> 00:06:03,267
because it's vintage.

131
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:05,933
I don't really like it.

132
00:06:06,067 --> 00:06:10,367
Besides, there are newer,
better ones out there.

133
00:06:10,533 --> 00:06:11,700
Old?

134
00:06:11,833 --> 00:06:13,000
Antique?

135
00:06:14,133 --> 00:06:15,600
Maybe you mean timeless,

136
00:06:15,733 --> 00:06:17,700
the kind you'll always
come back to.

137
00:06:20,167 --> 00:06:22,967
How about you?
What do you prefer?

138
00:06:23,100 --> 00:06:26,367
Antique, old, or...

139
00:06:26,500 --> 00:06:28,133
new?

140
00:06:31,133 --> 00:06:33,833
Wait, are we still
talking about clothes?

141
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:36,433
You know what, Babe?

142
00:06:36,567 --> 00:06:43,867
If you don't like anything here,
we can look in other stores.

143
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:47,933
Right, right.

144
00:06:48,067 --> 00:06:49,767
- Let's go.
- Come on.

145
00:06:49,900 --> 00:06:51,533
<i>I don't really like
the clothes here.</i>

146
00:06:51,667 --> 00:06:53,767
They're not so fresh.

147
00:06:53,900 --> 00:06:55,433
- Thank you, Ma'am!
- Thank you!

148
00:06:55,567 --> 00:06:56,633
Thank you.

149
00:06:57,833 --> 00:06:59,300
Are you okay...

150
00:06:59,433 --> 00:07:00,367
Babe?

151
00:07:02,233 --> 00:07:05,500
Even if pretending is hard,
I'll still do it.

152
00:07:05,633 --> 00:07:08,200
Because it's for my father.
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

153
00:07:08,333 --> 00:07:10,033
Right, Babe?

154
00:07:10,167 --> 00:07:11,533
Right?

155
00:07:11,667 --> 00:07:12,667
Right?

156
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:15,067
Let's go!

157
00:07:15,233 --> 00:07:16,400
Let's...

158
00:07:17,633 --> 00:07:19,567
<i>Hey, you pay for this later,
okay?</i>

159
00:07:24,800 --> 00:07:26,933
You think I'm outdated?

160
00:07:27,067 --> 00:07:29,400
But I can guarantee you...

161
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:31,733
Andrew will come back to me.

162
00:07:33,133 --> 00:07:35,867
Berdugo seems okay,
Madam Delilah.

163
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,300
Imagine, he had
the decency to call

164
00:07:38,433 --> 00:07:42,400
and confirm your meeting.

165
00:07:42,533 --> 00:07:44,367
I approve of him too,

166
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:48,200
because I think he really
means business, Ma'am.

167
00:07:48,367 --> 00:07:51,867
But, Boss, the name “Berdugo”
doesn't quite fit.

168
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:55,767
From his voice alone,
he sounds like a nice criminal.

169
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:57,467
Well...

170
00:07:57,600 --> 00:07:59,767
He seems to be a nice guy,

171
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:02,333
but I heard
he could be ruthless.

172
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:04,800
So...

173
00:08:04,933 --> 00:08:07,867
this deal must push through.

174
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Do you mean more ruthless
than you?

175
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:17,733
That's why I don't want us
to test who's more savage.

176
00:08:17,867 --> 00:08:22,867
So, this transaction
must be smooth...

177
00:08:23,033 --> 00:08:24,500
for our success.

178
00:08:25,667 --> 00:08:27,267
Well...

179
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:30,567
I'll just update you
on what happens, okay?

180
00:08:30,700 --> 00:08:33,467
- Sure, Madam.
- I'll see you.

181
00:08:33,600 --> 00:08:35,300
[FOREBODING MUSIC CONTINUES]

182
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:42,800
<i>Who are you?
What are you doing here?</i>

183
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:47,100
Oh, delivery.

184
00:08:47,233 --> 00:08:48,400
Who's this for?

185
00:08:48,533 --> 00:08:50,933
For Ara?

186
00:08:51,067 --> 00:08:53,833
That's mine.
I've been waiting for this.

187
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:54,867
Thank you.

188
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,333
You're welcome.

189
00:08:57,033 --> 00:08:58,467
Hey, thief!

190
00:08:58,600 --> 00:09:00,100
Wait, wait! He's not a thief!

191
00:09:00,233 --> 00:09:01,967
He just delivered my package.

192
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,067
Are you sure he was the one
who took your helmet?

193
00:09:04,200 --> 00:09:05,600
Yes, he took my helmet!

194
00:09:05,733 --> 00:09:07,333
Come on, let's go after him!

195
00:09:07,467 --> 00:09:08,800
Hurry!

196
00:09:08,933 --> 00:09:10,900
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

197
00:09:21,733 --> 00:09:23,100
It's over, you're finished.

198
00:09:23,233 --> 00:09:24,667
Nothing's missing.

199
00:09:24,800 --> 00:09:26,467
I just borrowed your helmet!

200
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,767
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

201
00:09:29,833 --> 00:09:32,233
Nothing missing?
You took my stuff!

202
00:09:32,367 --> 00:09:33,800
What's going on there?

203
00:09:33,933 --> 00:09:36,867
Never mind, the security
will take care of it.

204
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,067
Come on.

205
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:40,300
Better come with us.

206
00:09:42,033 --> 00:09:43,667
Explain yourself to the police.

207
00:09:43,800 --> 00:09:45,700
You've got nowhere to run!

208
00:09:45,833 --> 00:09:47,067
[GRUNTS]

209
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:49,200
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

210
00:09:52,733 --> 00:09:54,467
[CAR REVVING]

211
00:09:58,233 --> 00:10:00,567
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

212
00:10:02,433 --> 00:10:07,300
[TRICYCLE REVVING]

213
00:10:14,833 --> 00:10:15,967
May I buy?

214
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:17,033
Wait a second!

215
00:10:17,167 --> 00:10:19,367
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

216
00:10:19,500 --> 00:10:20,433
I'd like to buy!

217
00:10:20,567 --> 00:10:22,467
I said wait!

218
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:24,600
- Hey!
- Hey!

219
00:10:24,733 --> 00:10:26,433
- It's me!
- Big brother!

220
00:10:26,567 --> 00:10:28,667
Keith, come on! Come out here!

221
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:32,767
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

222
00:10:32,900 --> 00:10:34,467
Peter!

223
00:10:34,633 --> 00:10:35,700
How are you?

224
00:10:35,833 --> 00:10:38,467
I missed you! It's been so long!
[GROWLS]

225
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:40,433
You've grown taller.
How are you?

226
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:43,100
- Boom!
- Boom!

227
00:10:43,233 --> 00:10:44,767
You still haven't changed.

228
00:10:44,900 --> 00:10:46,467
Still lazy.
Always on your phone,

229
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,700
that's why our store
isn't earning.

230
00:10:48,833 --> 00:10:49,900
Peter, just this time.

231
00:10:50,033 --> 00:10:51,800
You too, you haven't changed.

232
00:10:51,933 --> 00:10:53,233
Still a nuisance.
[BABBLES]

233
00:10:53,367 --> 00:10:54,967
- You're crazy! Take this!
- Hey! My hair!

234
00:10:55,100 --> 00:10:57,467
- Your hair...
- But we're still the same,

235
00:10:57,600 --> 00:10:59,867
- handsome as ever.
- Handsome as ever!

236
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,800
Of course, we're both like that.

237
00:11:02,933 --> 00:11:05,100
Brother, my crush
liked my comment!

238
00:11:05,233 --> 00:11:06,700
She liked my comment! Look!

239
00:11:06,833 --> 00:11:08,167
- There, there. Read it.
- Wait, wait.

240
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:10,000
Yes, I saw it.

241
00:11:10,133 --> 00:11:11,533
I've had a crush on her
for so long.

242
00:11:11,667 --> 00:11:12,900
But it's the first time
she posted a comment.

243
00:11:13,033 --> 00:11:15,067
I'm so shy.

244
00:11:15,200 --> 00:11:17,100
You're being shy?

245
00:11:17,233 --> 00:11:20,467
So, you're shy,
that's where we're different.

246
00:11:20,600 --> 00:11:23,500
If you like someone, tell her!

247
00:11:23,633 --> 00:11:25,800
Show her! Shout it out!

248
00:11:25,933 --> 00:11:27,000
Don't be shy.

249
00:11:27,133 --> 00:11:28,133
Is that what you did?

250
00:11:28,267 --> 00:11:29,700
Yes!

251
00:11:29,833 --> 00:11:30,767
So...

252
00:11:30,900 --> 00:11:31,800
are you together now?

253
00:11:31,933 --> 00:11:33,167
Is she your girlfriend?

254
00:11:34,600 --> 00:11:35,967
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

255
00:11:36,100 --> 00:11:38,633
- Well, she's kind of slippery.
- Okay.

256
00:11:38,767 --> 00:11:39,667
We're almost there.

257
00:11:39,800 --> 00:11:41,767
[CHUCKLES]

258
00:11:41,933 --> 00:11:42,967
There.

259
00:11:45,867 --> 00:11:49,567
Wow, this is so beautiful!

260
00:11:49,700 --> 00:11:51,167
Boss.

261
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:52,733
So...

262
00:11:52,867 --> 00:11:54,167
Do you like it?

263
00:11:54,300 --> 00:11:56,367
The lights, the setup,
the service...

264
00:11:56,500 --> 00:11:57,700
Is this setup okay for you?

265
00:11:57,833 --> 00:11:58,800
Yes.

266
00:11:58,933 --> 00:12:00,733
Super romantic.

267
00:12:00,867 --> 00:12:04,133
I'm sure this is what you do
with your other girls too.

268
00:12:07,633 --> 00:12:10,433
No, I don't do this,
especially not for guests.

269
00:12:10,567 --> 00:12:11,467
Oh, my!

270
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:13,667
I'm sure that's what
you tell them too.

271
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,233
[CHUCKLES]

272
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:17,633
Food's ready!

273
00:12:21,933 --> 00:12:23,600
Joey...
[DREAMY MUSIC PLAYING]

274
00:12:23,733 --> 00:12:24,767
Cooked.

275
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:25,867
Okay.

276
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:27,700
It's still hot.

277
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,733
Boss Idol!

278
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:32,967
You're also here!

279
00:12:33,100 --> 00:12:34,267
Zoey...

280
00:12:35,467 --> 00:12:37,300
But how come you're alone?

281
00:12:41,833 --> 00:12:43,533
Actually, he's not alone.

282
00:12:44,567 --> 00:12:46,733
[DREAMY MUSIC CONTINUES]

283
00:12:56,167 --> 00:12:58,933
Wow! So my brother
has a girlfriend now!

284
00:12:59,067 --> 00:13:01,100
Is that why you came home,
to introduce her to us?

285
00:13:01,233 --> 00:13:03,267
You talk too much.
Here, carry my things.

286
00:13:03,400 --> 00:13:04,733
- Let's go.
- Let's go.

287
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,367
You talk too much.

288
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,833
- Hey!
- Peter!

289
00:13:08,967 --> 00:13:09,900
- Peter, Peter!
- Auntie Beng!

290
00:13:10,033 --> 00:13:11,367
Peter!

291
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,867
[GROWLING]

292
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:13,967
Put me down.

293
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,367
That's enough.

294
00:13:16,567 --> 00:13:17,833
- Auntie Bebeng!
- Auntie Beng!

295
00:13:17,967 --> 00:13:20,200
What's this? Right!
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

296
00:13:20,333 --> 00:13:21,467
How are you?

297
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:23,233
What can I say?
Why do you have a big bag?

298
00:13:23,367 --> 00:13:24,500
- Auntie!
- Oh, your auntie horsey!

299
00:13:24,633 --> 00:13:25,900
Stop teasing me.

300
00:13:26,033 --> 00:13:28,567
Auntie, I thought he'd come home
with his own family.

301
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:30,533
Why? Is he going abroad?

302
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:31,667
Oh, my God,
I don't know with you!

303
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:33,733
Come on! The food might burn!

304
00:13:33,867 --> 00:13:35,200
Let's go inside.

305
00:13:35,333 --> 00:13:37,167
Hey! Hey, get inside!

306
00:13:37,300 --> 00:13:38,800
- Hey!
- Oh, I'm coming!

307
00:13:38,933 --> 00:13:39,967
Let's go.

308
00:13:41,167 --> 00:13:42,067
[GRUNTS]

309
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:46,267
Wow, your cooking
smells delicious.

310
00:13:47,300 --> 00:13:48,833
Let's eat. Oh...

311
00:13:48,967 --> 00:13:50,200
come join us.

312
00:13:51,267 --> 00:13:52,767
Oh, no...

313
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:53,833
No, thanks.

314
00:13:53,967 --> 00:13:57,033
Francis prepared something
for our date tonight.

315
00:13:58,467 --> 00:14:00,100
- Okay.
- But it's a shame,

316
00:14:00,233 --> 00:14:03,167
I cooked a lot.

317
00:14:03,300 --> 00:14:05,367
She's right. You can have some.

318
00:14:05,500 --> 00:14:06,367
Right?

319
00:14:06,500 --> 00:14:08,133
Oh, no, don't bother.
[CHUCKLES]

320
00:14:08,267 --> 00:14:09,200
So? Shall we go?

321
00:14:09,333 --> 00:14:11,867
You must be Joey, right?

322
00:14:12,000 --> 00:14:14,367
Madam Delilah
entrusted you to me.

323
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,333
If you need anything,
just let me know, okay?

324
00:14:17,467 --> 00:14:19,233
- Thank you very much.
- Thanks.

325
00:14:20,233 --> 00:14:21,600
So? Shall we go?

326
00:14:21,733 --> 00:14:23,933
Let's head to our tent.
I like ours better.

327
00:14:24,067 --> 00:14:25,433
All right.

328
00:14:25,567 --> 00:14:26,867
Okay.

329
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,100
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

330
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,767
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

331
00:14:38,733 --> 00:14:40,500
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

332
00:14:50,567 --> 00:14:51,833
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

333
00:14:51,967 --> 00:14:53,700
- Plate.
- Thanks.

334
00:14:54,800 --> 00:14:57,767
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

335
00:15:22,133 --> 00:15:24,433
[CHUCKLES]

336
00:15:27,867 --> 00:15:30,833
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

337
00:15:32,667 --> 00:15:34,900
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

338
00:15:35,067 --> 00:15:36,500
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]

339
00:15:37,667 --> 00:15:38,667
Cheers?

340
00:15:39,633 --> 00:15:41,800
- [CLINKS]
- [CHUCKLES]

341
00:15:46,033 --> 00:15:47,900
[CHUCKLES]

342
00:15:48,033 --> 00:15:49,600
Are you enjoying yourself?

343
00:15:49,733 --> 00:15:52,700
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

344
00:16:03,200 --> 00:16:04,433
Like this?

345
00:16:12,500 --> 00:16:14,000
Clarissa.

346
00:16:14,133 --> 00:16:16,967
This is my mother, Rebecca.

347
00:16:17,100 --> 00:16:18,433
Mom...

348
00:16:18,567 --> 00:16:20,133
this is Clarissa.

349
00:16:20,267 --> 00:16:22,300
She works in our foundation,

350
00:16:22,433 --> 00:16:27,567
and she offered
to be your caregiver.

351
00:16:30,233 --> 00:16:32,000
Good evening, Ma'am.

352
00:16:34,600 --> 00:16:37,733
You're applying as a caregiver?

353
00:16:37,867 --> 00:16:39,200
Can you handle it?

354
00:16:40,767 --> 00:16:42,067
Yes, Ma'am.

355
00:16:42,233 --> 00:16:43,600
I used to be a nurse.

356
00:16:43,733 --> 00:16:46,633
But I didn't continue.

357
00:16:49,167 --> 00:16:51,233
Why did you give up your career?

358
00:16:51,367 --> 00:16:53,933
I chose my family instead.

359
00:16:54,333 --> 00:16:57,400
I chose to be a mother
rather than pursue the job.

360
00:17:00,833 --> 00:17:02,200
So...

361
00:17:02,333 --> 00:17:05,667
that means,
if your family needs you,

362
00:17:05,800 --> 00:17:10,267
you might leave this job, right?

363
00:17:10,400 --> 00:17:12,333
No, Ma'am.

364
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:16,533
My husband has already
passed away.

365
00:17:16,700 --> 00:17:18,300
- Mom...
- Yes?

366
00:17:18,433 --> 00:17:21,967
I forgot to tell you
that her husband just died.

367
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:24,600
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

368
00:17:26,633 --> 00:17:28,433
I'm sorry.

369
00:17:28,567 --> 00:17:30,067
I'm sorry.

370
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,833
It's okay, Ma'am.

371
00:17:32,100 --> 00:17:35,367
Maybe that's why I applied
to Ma'am Yvette

372
00:17:35,500 --> 00:17:38,400
to be your caregiver because...

373
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:42,100
I miss having someone
to look after and care for.

374
00:17:42,233 --> 00:17:45,033
But I won't leave you.

375
00:17:45,267 --> 00:17:46,800
Ma'am Yvette has been
so kind to me.

376
00:17:46,933 --> 00:17:50,100
I don't want to break the trust
she's given me.

377
00:17:52,500 --> 00:17:55,133
I'm hungry.

378
00:17:55,267 --> 00:17:56,400
Okay, let's eat, Mom.

379
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:57,667
Sit down.

380
00:17:59,667 --> 00:18:02,633
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

381
00:18:16,233 --> 00:18:18,967
Why don't you join us?

382
00:18:19,100 --> 00:18:22,200
Don't tell me that once
you start taking care of me,

383
00:18:22,367 --> 00:18:24,767
you'll still be shy.

384
00:18:24,900 --> 00:18:26,467
Clarissa, join us.

385
00:18:27,800 --> 00:18:29,933
Sit down.

386
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:32,167
All right, thank you.

387
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:37,367
What time will you
arrive tomorrow?

388
00:18:37,500 --> 00:18:40,000
I have a morning routine.

389
00:18:40,133 --> 00:18:41,100
Oh, Mom.

390
00:18:41,233 --> 00:18:44,267
Clarissa is never late.

391
00:18:44,400 --> 00:18:46,200
Good.

392
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:47,600
You want rice?

393
00:18:49,133 --> 00:18:50,400
Thank you.

394
00:18:50,533 --> 00:18:53,500
[UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING]

395
00:18:56,567 --> 00:18:58,100
Hey, you're always
on your cell phone.

396
00:18:58,233 --> 00:19:00,200
Someone might be buying
at our store.

397
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:02,233
Brother, they don't need
to shout.

398
00:19:02,567 --> 00:19:04,433
We've got a buzzer now.

399
00:19:04,667 --> 00:19:06,533
You've been away for so long.

400
00:19:06,667 --> 00:19:07,700
Well...

401
00:19:07,967 --> 00:19:09,767
I thought you'd settle down
there.

402
00:19:11,200 --> 00:19:12,667
That's just what you thought.

403
00:19:12,800 --> 00:19:15,067
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING]

404
00:19:15,300 --> 00:19:17,067
So why did you really come home,
Brother?

405
00:19:18,667 --> 00:19:20,500
Looks like you brought
all your things.

406
00:19:21,733 --> 00:19:23,067
I just want to forget something.

407
00:19:23,200 --> 00:19:25,233
Forget?

408
00:19:25,367 --> 00:19:26,867
What?

409
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:29,367
I mean, who?

410
00:19:31,300 --> 00:19:32,667
Never mind.

411
00:19:32,800 --> 00:19:34,267
You ask too many questions.

412
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,933
Of course, you're my brother!

413
00:19:36,067 --> 00:19:37,700
I worry about you.

414
00:19:38,900 --> 00:19:40,433
But fine.

415
00:19:40,567 --> 00:19:43,567
Whoever or whatever it is,

416
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,100
I'll help you forget.

417
00:19:46,233 --> 00:19:47,133
Really?

418
00:19:47,267 --> 00:19:48,867
I can handle it.

419
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:51,233
Okay, if you say so.

420
00:19:56,733 --> 00:19:58,600
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

421
00:20:06,500 --> 00:20:08,200
<i> Ouch! Ouch!</i>

422
00:20:08,333 --> 00:20:10,333
<i>What's your problem?
[GROANS]</i>

423
00:20:10,467 --> 00:20:12,233
<i>I'm more likely to get injured
because of you.</i>

424
00:20:12,367 --> 00:20:15,467
<i>You're pretending,
but you're really hurt.</i>

425
00:20:15,600 --> 00:20:16,833
[CLACKS]

426
00:20:16,967 --> 00:20:19,933
[SENTIMENTAL MUSIC CONTINUES]

427
00:20:31,600 --> 00:20:33,267
You don't know
how to eat with your hands?

428
00:20:33,400 --> 00:20:35,633
What? I do!

429
00:20:35,800 --> 00:20:37,000
Look.

430
00:20:37,133 --> 00:20:38,467
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

431
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:40,300
- See?
- [CHUCKLES]

432
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:44,200
Just admit it,
you don't know how.

433
00:20:46,933 --> 00:20:48,600
Okay, fine.

434
00:20:48,733 --> 00:20:50,200
I don't know how.

435
00:20:50,333 --> 00:20:51,867
It shows.

436
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:53,900
Why? How do you do it? Teach me.

437
00:20:54,033 --> 00:20:55,500
It's like this.

438
00:20:56,733 --> 00:20:59,533
You're eating it like bread.

439
00:20:59,667 --> 00:21:01,267
No, like this.

440
00:21:01,400 --> 00:21:02,267
There...

441
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:04,200
- Okay.
- Get the viand,

442
00:21:04,333 --> 00:21:05,967
then add rice, like that.

443
00:21:06,100 --> 00:21:08,133
Then, see...

444
00:21:08,300 --> 00:21:11,267
[PLAYFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

445
00:21:13,867 --> 00:21:14,967
Wait.

446
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,433
You've got something
on your face.

447
00:21:16,567 --> 00:21:19,533
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

448
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:30,867
You know what?
[CHUCKLES]

449
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,200
You're not just sweet,
you're funny too.

450
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:35,333
[CHUCKLES]

451
00:21:37,633 --> 00:21:39,433
[CHUCKLES]

452
00:21:39,567 --> 00:21:42,533
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

453
00:21:48,633 --> 00:21:50,500
Your ex is really good,
isn't she?

454
00:21:52,967 --> 00:21:54,067
What do you mean?

455
00:21:55,033 --> 00:21:57,067
Well...

456
00:21:57,200 --> 00:21:59,400
even if we know
she's just pretending,

457
00:21:59,533 --> 00:22:01,700
you're still affected
by what she does.

458
00:22:05,900 --> 00:22:08,300
Do you still love her?

459
00:22:08,433 --> 00:22:11,400
[STIRRING ROMANTIC MUSIC
PLAYING]

460
00:22:24,700 --> 00:22:27,667
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

461
00:22:31,967 --> 00:22:34,200
I'd like to buy four shampoos.

462
00:22:34,333 --> 00:22:35,633
Looks like my crush
likes someone else.

463
00:22:35,767 --> 00:22:38,067
You should find out
what her interests are.

464
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:41,467
Theresa, when do I meet
your business partner?

465
00:22:41,600 --> 00:22:43,833
150,000 Lumen-X pills

466
00:22:43,967 --> 00:22:46,467
are on their way to Valmora
as we speak.

467
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:47,733
Excuse me, my boss is calling.

468
00:22:47,867 --> 00:22:50,300
I'm confirming
Berdugo is on his way.

469
00:22:50,467 --> 00:22:51,333
Everything is ready.

470
00:22:51,467 --> 00:22:53,300
I just want to know...

471
00:22:53,433 --> 00:22:54,533
are you and Joey together?

472
00:22:54,667 --> 00:22:55,800
We're just pretending, okay?

473
00:22:55,933 --> 00:22:57,800
I want you back, Andrew.

474
00:23:01,500 --> 00:23:03,367
<i> ♪ I will face it</i>

475
00:23:03,500 --> 00:23:07,233
<i> Never, never say die ♪</i>
